# Normalise line endings so they no longer depend on each contributor's Git
# config. Without this, a contributor on Linux or macOS -- where core.autocrlf
# defaults to false rather than Git for Windows' true -- commits whatever
# endings their editor produced, turning a one-line change into a whole-file
# diff for everyone else.
#
# text=auto stores LF and checks out native endings, so Windows working copies
# still get CRLF and nothing changes about how you edit.
#
# Deliberately added WITHOUT `git add --renormalize`. text=auto does not convert
# files that were already committed with CRLF, so the handful of files in this
# repository that carry CRLF keep it, no rewrite lands here, and those files
# stay byte-compatible with the same files upstream. Renormalising them would be
# a separate, deliberate decision.
* text=auto

# Assets, marked explicitly rather than relying on content detection.
*.png binary
